      "claim": "L4 nepicastat, a close cyclic-thiourea analog, is highly permeable across Caco-2 and MDCK-II monolayers (Papp ~5.3-5.4 × 10^-5 cm/s); lorcaserin, a small lipophilic basic chloroarene, is highly permeable (Papp ~30-37 × 10^-6 cm/s) with no P-gp substrate behavior; UC-781, domperidone, desloratadine, and indapamide show high permeability or near-complete absorption.",
